{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Review Core Engine Write Operations",
  "description": "Before writing to core engine files, reviews the proposed changes to ensure they follow framework patterns, maintain backward compatibility, and don't break the CustomWorld dependency injection.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "preToolUse",
    "toolTypes": [
      "write"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A write operation is about to modify a file. If the target is in src/core/ or src/hooks/, please verify:\n\n1. The change maintains backward compatibility with existing step definitions\n2. Any new engine follows the pattern: class with constructor, injected via CustomWorld\n3. Imports use the project's path aliases (@core/, @utils/, @config/, @steps/, @pages/)\n4. Error handling follows the framework's Logger pattern (Logger.info/warn/error)\n5. New exports are properly added to any barrel/index files if they exist\n6. The change doesn't introduce circular dependencies\n\nIf the file is NOT in src/core/ or src/hooks/, this check passes - proceed with the write."
  }
}